    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62915" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λῆμνος</span></b> , ἡ, 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λᾶμνος</span></b> , <u>Lemnos</u>,
			<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			1.593
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			Od.
			8.283
		</span></i>; sacred to Hephaestus, Sch.<i><span class="en">
			A.R.
			1.851
		</span></i>, etc.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαμνόθεν</span></b> ,
			Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>from Lemnos</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.52
			</span></i>:—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λήμνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
				<u>Lemnian</u>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					800
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				299
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λ. ἔργα</span>, prov. from the
			wickedness of certain Lemnian women, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.138
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				631
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λ. ἄμπελοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pax</u>
					1162
				</span></i>
			:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λημνιακός</span></b> , 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαμν</span></b> - <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1.44
			</span></i> P.:—also fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λημνιάς </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαμνιάς</span></b> ), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				4.22
			</span></i>; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λημνίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, μίλτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					865
				</span></i>
			.</div>
